  "body": "With the local model set to AstrLink Guard (#3578), the eval case `token-count` in internal/redact/eval_cases_test.go comes out wrong:\n\n```\n<system-reminder><total_tokens>14902266 tokens left</total_tokens></system-reminder>\n```\n\nThe model labels `14902266` `common_secret` (magpie's `secret`, span 31..39 in testdata/eval-astrlink.json), and redact's checks keep it, so it is masked. Privacy Filter labels the same value an account number, which the checks already drop.\n\nRules alone: kept. AstrLink Guard raw: secret. Rules + AstrLink Guard: masked (wrong).\n\nThe case carries `GuardKnown` pointing here; it fails once this is fixed, to have that taken off. A likely fix is in redact's checks on a model secret (a bare decimal count next to a word that says it counts something), not the model.",
