   "body": "Fixed on a fork branch: `fix/3775-token-count` (head `c4fd6c4b`, on upstream `6afbe3f3`) — a token count inside `<total_tokens>` is no secret to the local model.\n\n**Root cause.** `internal/redact/model.go`'s `case \"SECRET\"` in `modelFits` lets a long bare digit run through when the model calls it secret — nothing there tells a count from a value.\n\n**Change.** a veto before the final return: a value that is all digits with a counting cue near it (tokens, count, total, left, remaining, items, rows — the existing `cued` helper and a new cue list) is not a secret. A numeric password with no counting word near it stays masked, and so does one in `password = \"…\"`. The eval's `GuardKnown: \"#3775\"` comes off with it.\n\n**Verified.** Red: `go test -tags nogui ./internal/redact/ -run TestModelCountIsNoSecret` → `model_test.go:166: \"14902266\" gone from \"<system-reminder><total_tokens>14902266 tokens left</total_tokens></system-reminder>\"`\nGreen: `same command → 5/5; eval green with the marker off; package's 92 tests pass` → `ok github.com/yetone/magpie/internal/redact`\n\nLimit worth knowing: the cues are substring matches, so an all-digit model \"secret\" within 40 bytes of e.g. \"discount\" is kept unmasked too. Narrowing them to word boundaries is a one-line change if you'd rather have that.\n\nFull `go test -tags nogui ./...` over round 26's branches: 70 packages ok, 5 red (edit `TestWriteAtomicReadOnlyHardLink`, gateway's five, plugin `TestPluginSOCKSProxy`, provider's synctest fatal in `TestUnreadLoginsWriteErrorsKeepCredentials`, testenv `TestProgram`) — every one of them reproduces identically at base `6afbe3f3` in this environment (umask 0027), so none is from this change.\n\nBranch: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3775-token-count — no PR opened, this repo takes no external PRs; say the word if you'd rather have the patch inline here.",
